    "description": "# Future Directions \u2014 Analogy as a Mathematical Operation\n\nThe discrete model developed in this cycle scores an analogy `(fwd, bwd)` between\nfinite carriers by the number of concepts its round trip returns unchanged. We\nestablished that the maximisers are exactly the split monomorphisms (permutations,\nin the self-finite case), that the identity (\"Copycat\") analogy is one maximiser\namong many, that a two-sided score is maximal precisely for bijections, and that\nweighting concepts and composing analogies both respect this extremal structure.\nThese results suggest the following bold, testable conjectures.\n\n## 1. Categorical lift preserves the maximiser dichotomy\n\nReplace carriers by finite categories and the maps by functors `F : A \u2964 B`,\n`G : B \u2964 A`, scoring the analogy by how close `G \u2218 F` is to the identity functor\n(number of objects fixed up to isomorphism, or the isomorphism defect of the\ncounit). **Conjecture:** one-sided maximisers are exactly the functors admitting\na retraction (categorical split monomorphisms), and two-sided maximisers are\nexactly the equivalences of categories.\n\n*The key insight is* that the fixed-point count of the discrete round trip is the\nobject-level shadow of the counit `G \u2218 F \u21d2 id`, so \"fixed concept\" becomes\n\"object where the counit is an isomorphism,\" and split-mono/equivalence survives\nverbatim. *Why now?* The discrete base case has been pinned down exactly, so the\nonly new ingredient is bookkeeping of natural isomorphisms \u2014 the extremal\ncombinatorics is already understood.\n\n## 2. Weighted fidelity is optimised by a maximum-weight partial matching\n\nAttach nonnegative weights to concepts and to preserved relations, and maximise\nthe weighted count over all admissible analogies. **Conjecture:** the optimal\none-sided analogy is computed by a maximum-weight partial injection (an\nassignment problem), so the optimum is attained, is polynomial-time computable,\nand is monotone and submodular in the weight vector.\n\n*The key insight is* that a one-sided maximiser only needs its forward map to be\ninjective on the fixed set, turning fidelity maximisation into a bipartite\nmatching whose value is the optimum of a totally unimodular program. *Why now?*\nMonotonicity in the weights is already proved, which is the hypothesis that lets\nthe greedy/matching machinery certify global optimality.\n\n## 3. The two-sided score metrises the \"distance from equivalence\"\n\nDefine `d(\u03c6) = (|A| + |B|) \u2212 twoSided(\u03c6)`. **Conjecture:** `d` is a genuine\npremetric on analogies whose zero set is exactly the equivalences, and it obeys a\ncomposition inequality `d(\u03c8 \u2218 \u03c6) \u2264 d(\u03c8) + d(\u03c6)`, making analogies with this cost\ninto a Lawvere-style enriched structure.\n\n*The key insight is* that two-sided maximality already characterises bijections,\nso the residual `d` measures precisely the failure of surjectivity on each side,\nand failures can only accumulate additively under composition. *Why now?* Both\nthe exact zero-set characterisation and the preservation of perfection under\ncomposition are in hand, giving the triangle inequality's two endpoints.\n\n## 4. Metric fidelity admits minimisers with a quantitative composition bound\n\nFor finite metric carriers, replace the fixed-point count by the maximal\ndisplacement `max_a d(bwd(fwd(a)), a)` of the round trip. **Conjecture:** a\nminimiser exists over any finite family of candidate analogies, the minimal\ndisplacement is zero exactly for the perfect analogies of the discrete model, and\ndisplacements compose subadditively: the round-trip displacement of `\u03c8 \u2218 \u03c6` is\nbounded by a Lipschitz-weighted sum of the individual displacements.\n\n*The key insight is* that the discrete perfect analogies are the zero-displacement\ncore, so the metric theory is a continuous relaxation whose minimum recovers the\ncombinatorial optimum. *Why now?* Finiteness gives existence of minimisers for\nfree, and the composition law for perfect analogies is the exact `displacement =\n0` case of the conjectured inequality.\n\n## 5. Maximisers form a groupoid, and self-maximisers a group\n\n**Conjecture:** the two-sided maximisers (equivalences) between carriers form a\ngroupoid under composition, whose isotropy at a single carrier is its\nautomorphism group; in the self-finite case this recovers the symmetric group,\nand the one-sided maximisers form its associated monoid of split idempotents.\n\n*The key insight is* that composition preserves perfection and Copycat is a\ntwo-sided unit, so maximisers are already closed under the operations that define\na groupoid \u2014 only invertibility of each two-sided maximiser remains, which is\nexactly the extracted equivalence. *Why now?* The unit laws and composition\nclosure are proved, so the algebraic structure is one invertibility lemma away.\n",
