    "description": "# Future Directions\n\nThe following conjectures are concrete extensions of the formally verified algebraic results in `Catalog/Computation/DeterminantValuesOnLattices.lean`. Each is falsifiable by an explicit lattice or by failure of the stated limit.\n\n1. **Effective error term for algebraic determinant lattices.** For every `d \u2265 2` and every full lattice `\u039b \u2282 M_d(\u211d)` with algebraic entries whose determinant values are not contained in `c\u2124` for any real `c`, there exists `\u03b4 = \u03b4(\u039b) > 0` such that, for fixed `a < b`, the nonzero determinant count in the Frobenius ball differs from its main term by `O_{\u039b,a,b}(T^{d(d-1)-\u03b4})`.\n\n2. **Uniformity over moving determinant windows.** Under the same hypotheses, there is an exponent `\u03b7_d > 0` such that the asymptotic remains valid uniformly for intervals `[a_T,b_T]` contained in a fixed compact set and satisfying `b_T-a_T \u2265 T^{-\u03b7_d}`.\n\n3. **Sharp determinant\u2013energy inequality in every dimension.** For every `d \u2265 2` and every real `d \u00d7 d` matrix `M`, `d * |det M|^(2/d) \u2264 squareEnergy M`; equality holds exactly when `M\u1d40M` is a nonnegative scalar multiple of the identity. The file proves the inequality and sharpness family when `d = 2`, but not the equality classification.\n\n4. **Density dichotomy for algebraic matrix lattices.** If `\u039b \u2282 M_d(\u211d)` is a full lattice with algebraic entries, then the additive subgroup generated by `{det v | v \u2208 \u039b}` is either discrete cyclic or dense in `\u211d`; in the dense case, every nonempty open interval contains a nonzero determinant value.\n\n5. **Zero-determinant asymptotic for all diagonal lattices.** For every `d \u2265 4`, every full diagonal deformation of the standard matrix lattice satisfies the isotropic noncoincidence condition and has a determinant-zero counting asymptotic with exponent `d(d-1)` and a positive leading constant.\n",
