    "consumed_by_exp_id": "",
    "description": "# Future directions\n\n## Corrected mathematical status\n\nThe proposed powers-of-two family is a **strictly descending**, separated\nfiltration, not an ascending chain.  The formal development proves this both\nfor the function ring `\u2124 \u2192 \u2124` and for the actual ring of integer-valued\npolynomials\n\\[\n\\operatorname{Int}(\\mathbb Z)=\\{p\\in\\mathbb Q[X]:p(\\mathbb Z)\\subseteq\\mathbb Z\\}.\n\\]\nConsequently it does not establish an \u201cEscher staircase\u201d in the stated sense.\nMoreover, requiring zero to belong to the intersection does not add a loop:\nzero belongs to every ideal.\n\nFinite-variable polynomial rings over fields are Noetherian, so they admit no\ninfinite strict ascending chain of ideals.  Their Krull dimension is `n`, but\nthat cannot equal the length of an infinite ascending ideal chain as proposed.\nThe same ascending-chain obstruction applies to any Noetherian ring, including\na discrete valuation ring.\n\n## Natural next formal results\n\n1. **General separated principal filtrations.** Replace `2 \u2208 \u2124` by an element\n   `a` in a domain and identify hypotheses under which `\u22c2 n, (a^n) = 0`.\n   This points toward the Krull intersection theorem rather than a new\n   ascending-chain invariant.\n\n2. **Non-Noetherian examples with genuine ascent.** Formalize standard strict\n   chains such as\n   `(x\u2081) \u228a (x\u2081,x\u2082) \u228a \u22ef` in a polynomial ring with countably many variables.\n   Such chains witness failure of ACC, but do not \u201cloop back.\u201d\n\n3. **Equivalence with Noetherianity.** Package the standard equivalence:\n   a commutative ring is Noetherian iff every monotone natural-number-indexed\n   chain of ideals stabilizes.  Its negation supplies a non-stabilizing\n   ascending chain, and a subsequence can be chosen strictly increasing.\n\n4. **Algebraic integers.** Before assigning a height, define a coherent\n   invariant.  The ring of all algebraic integers is non-Noetherian, so genuine\n   ascending chains can be studied there.  Possible established invariants to\n   compare include Krull dimension, valuative dimension, and lengths of prime\n   chains; none is presently identified with the proposed condition.\n\n5. **Formalize `Int(\u2124)` further.** Develop binomial-basis descriptions and the\n   ideals of polynomials whose fixed divisors are divisible by a prescribed\n   integer.  The current file provides a self-contained subring definition,\n   integer evaluation homomorphisms, strict filtration, and zero-intersection\n   theorem as a foundation.\n",
