    "description": "# Future Directions\n\nThe Lean development proves exact results for an explicit region-capacity model.  The following are concrete extensions that would connect those combinatorial bounds to analytic approximation and genuine network lower bounds.\n\n1. **Constructive width-`n+4` approximation.**  For every `n > 0`, continuous `f : (Fin n \u2192 \u211d) \u2192 \u211d`, and `\u03b5 > 0`, if `f` is restricted to the cube `[-1,1]^n`, there is a finite ReLU network with every hidden-layer width at most `n+4` whose uniform error is below `\u03b5`.  This is falsified by a continuous function and positive tolerance for which no such bounded-width network exists.\n\n2. **Lipschitz shallow upper rate.**  There is a dimension-dependent constant `C_n` such that every `K`-Lipschitz function on `[-1,1]^n` has a one-hidden-layer ReLU approximation of uniform error at most `\u03b5` and width at most `C_n * (K/\u03b5)^n`.  A family of normalized Lipschitz functions violating this width bound falsifies the conjecture.\n\n3. **No function-independent rate for mere continuity.**  For every proposed width bound `W : \u2115 \u2192 \u2115`, there are a continuous function on `[0,1]` and an integer `m > 0` such that every one-hidden-layer ReLU network of width at most `W m` has uniform error at least `1/m`.  A single bound working for all continuous functions falsifies this conjecture.\n\n4. **Tent-map linear-region separation.**  The `L`-fold iterate of the normalized tent map has exactly `2^L` maximal affine intervals, while every scalar depth-`D` ReLU network with widths `w\u2081,\u2026,w_D` has at most `\u220f i, (w\u1d62+1)` maximal affine intervals.  Either an incorrect exact count or a network exceeding the product bound falsifies the statement.\n\n5. **Depth-`L` lower bound from oscillations.**  There are explicit functions represented by depth `L+1` networks of size polynomial in `L` such that any depth-`L` ReLU network approximating them within a fixed uniform tolerance has size exponential in `L`.  A polynomial-size depth-`L` approximating family for the explicit witnesses falsifies the conjecture.\n",
