    "description": "# Future directions\n\nDerived from the five Lean files of this thread, all of which compile against\nmathlib4 (Lean 4.28.0) with no `sorry` and use only the standard axioms\n`propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`:\n\n* `Catalog/Applications/WallpaperRhythm/QuotientEntropy.lean` \u2014 the abstract\n  `InvariantPattern` capacity theorem (earlier cycle);\n* `Catalog/Computation/WallpaperRhythm/OrbitCounting.lean` \u2014 instantiation of\n  that setoid by a group action, Burnside evaluation, exact counts on the\n  toroidal grids `ZMod p \u00d7 ZMod q`;\n* `Catalog/Computation/WallpaperRhythm/OrbitEntropy.lean` \u2014 probabilistic\n  entropy, strict monotonicity of capacity, the `IsCanonAt` predicate with its\n  onset-count obstruction, the quarter-turn descent criterion;\n* `Catalog/Computation/WallpaperRhythm/QuarterTurnCapacity.lean` \u2014 realizability\n  of symmetry groups, the exact quarter-turn capacity of every square torus, and\n  the point-group descent dichotomy;\n* `Catalog/Computation/WallpaperRhythm/BernoulliEntropy.lean` \u2014 the exact entropy\n  of the orbit-Bernoulli model and the per-orbit entropy deficit;\n* `Catalog/Computation/WallpaperRhythm/CanonSharpness.lean` \u2014 the complete onset\n  spectrum of canons;\n* `Catalog/Computation/WallpaperRhythm/GlideCapacity.lean` \u2014 glide reflections of\n  a torus: fixed-point freeness and the capacity `2 ^ (p q / 2)`.\n\n## Status of the conjectures posed in the previous cycle\n\nAll five are now **theorems**.\n\n* **C1. Realizability of symmetry types \u2014 proved, and in greater generality.**\n  `symmetryGroup_subgroupPattern`: for the translation action of any group `G` on\n  itself, every subgroup `H \u2264 G` is *exactly* the symmetry group of the indicator\n  pattern of `H`.  `symmetryGroup_torusSubgroupPattern` transports this to the\n  cyclic time-shift action on the `p \u00d7 q` torus, so on a drum grid every\n  symmetry type is realized by an explicit pattern.\n* **C2. Sharpness of the canon onset obstruction \u2014 proved.**\n  `isCanonAt_onsetCount_iff`: a number `k` is the onset count of some canon at\n  time distance `g` on the `p \u00d7 q` torus **iff** `addOrderOf g \u2223 k` and\n  `k \u2264 p * q`.  The divisibility obstruction of the previous cycle is therefore\n  complete, not merely necessary.  The general mechanism is\n  `exists_invariant_finset_card` (a free action of a finite group has an\n  invariant subset of every size `|\u0393| \u00b7 j` with `j` at most the orbit count).\n  Worked instance: `canon_onsetCount_four_one` (`{0, 2, 4}` on the four-beat\n  grid).\n* **C3. Quarter-turn capacity \u2014 proved, and extended to even side lengths.**\n  `card_pattern_quarterTurn`: the number of quarter-turn invariant patterns on\n  the `p \u00d7 p` torus is `2 ^ ((p\u00b2 + 2t + t\u00b2) / 4)` with `t = twoTorsionCard p`.\n  For odd `p` this is the conjectured `2 ^ ((p\u00b2 + 3) / 4)`; for even `p` it is\n  `2 ^ ((p\u00b2 + 8) / 4)`, because the quarter turn then fixes two diagonal cells\n  and the half turn four.  Numeric instances: `8` (3\u00d73), `128` (5\u00d75), `8` (2\u00d72),\n  `64` (4\u00d74).\n* **C4. Which point groups descend to a rectangular torus \u2014 proved.**\n  `signedDiag_mapsTo_torusLattice` (diagonal sign changes always preserve\n  `p\u2124 \u00d7 q\u2124`) together with `signedSwap_mapsTo_torusLattice_iff` (a signed\n  coordinate swap preserves it iff `p = q`) determines the subgroup of the\n  order-eight point group `D\u2084` descending to the `p \u00d7 q` torus: the order-four\n  diagonal subgroup when `p \u2260 q`, all of `D\u2084` when `p = q`.\n* **C5. Entropy deficit as a measure of stylistic constraint \u2014 proved.**\n  `entropyBits_orbitBernoulli`: the orbit-Bernoulli distribution (switch each of\n  the `m` orbits on independently with probability `\u03b8`) has entropy exactly\n  `m \u00b7 H\u2082(\u03b8)` bits, so by `entropyDeficit_orbitBernoulli` the deficit is\n  `m \u00b7 (1 - H\u2082(\u03b8))` \u2014 a fixed cost per orbit \u2014 nonnegative\n  (`entropyDeficit_nonneg`) and zero exactly at `\u03b8 = 1/2`\n  (`entropyDeficit_eq_zero_iff`).\n\n## New conjectures\n\nEach is stated so that a single Lean counterexample refutes it.\n\n### N1. Capacity of a rectangular torus under its full descended point group\n\nBy C4 the point group descending to the `p \u00d7 q` torus with `p \u2260 q` is the Klein\nfour-group `{diag(\u00b11, \u00b11)}`.  Conjecture: the number of patterns invariant under\nall four of its elements is\n\n    2 ^ ( (p + t(p)) * (q + t(q)) / 4 ),   t(n) = twoTorsionCard n = gcd(2, n),\n\nsince Burnside adds `p*q`, `q*t(p)`, `p*t(q)` and `t(p)*t(q)` fixed cells.\n*Refutation:* a pair `(p, q)` where a brute-force count differs \u2014 equivalently a\ncell fixed by a coordinate sign change that the parity bookkeeping misses.\nThis is the rectangular counterpart of the proved `card_pattern_quarterTurn`, and\nwould complete the capacity table for every planar point group that descends.\n\n### N2. Capacity under the full dihedral group of a square torus\n\nFor `p` odd let `D\u2084` act on `ZMod p \u00d7 ZMod p` by the four rotations of\n`QuarterTurns` together with the four reflections `(t,n) \u21a6 (n,t)`,\n`(t,n) \u21a6 (-n,-t)`, `(t,n) \u21a6 (-t,n)`, `(t,n) \u21a6 (t,-n)`.  Each reflection should\nfix exactly `p` cells, so Burnside predicts `(p + 1)(p + 3) / 8` orbits and\n\n    capacity = 2 ^ ((p + 1) * (p + 3) / 8).\n\n*Refutation:* an odd `p` (say `p = 7`, predicted `2 ^ 10`) where the count\ndiffers.  Note the prediction agrees with the proved rotation-only value at\n`p = 3` (both give `8`) but is strictly smaller from `p = 5` on, so the two\nstatements are independent.\n\n### N3. Realizability for a non-free action\n\n`symmetryGroup_subgroupPattern` realizes every subgroup for a *free* translation\naction.  Conjecture: realizability survives the loss of freeness for the\nquarter-turn action \u2014 for every `p \u2265 3` and every subgroup `H \u2264 QuarterTurns`\nthere is a pattern `f : ZMod p \u00d7 ZMod p \u2192 Bool` with\n`symmetryGroup QuarterTurns f = H`.  *Refutation:* a `p \u2265 3` and a subgroup\n(necessarily one of `\u22a5`, the half-turn subgroup, `\u22a4`) realized by no pattern.\nFailure at `p = 1` is immediate \u2014 the single cell forces `\u22a4` \u2014 so the bound\n`p \u2265 3` is part of the claim.\n\n### N4. Capacity of the toroidal \"pg\" group\n\n`card_pattern_glide` counts the patterns invariant under a single glide\nreflection `\u03b3(t, n) = (t + p/2, -n)` on the `p \u00d7 q` torus with `p` even: there\nare `2 ^ (p q / 2)`, since `\u03b3` is fixed-point free\n(`fixedBy_glide_eq_empty`).  Conjecture: for the larger group generated by `\u03b3`\ntogether with *every* time shift \u2014 the toroidal analogue of the wallpaper group\n`pg` \u2014 the orbits are exactly the pitch pairs `{n, -n}`, so the capacity is\n\n    2 ^ ((q + t(q)) / 2),   t(n) = gcd(2, n),\n\nindependently of `p`.  *Refutation:* an even `p` and a `q` where a brute-force\ncount differs, i.e. where the glide and the shifts fail to merge two cells with\nthe same pitch class.  For `q = 3` the prediction is `4` patterns for every even\n`p`.\n\n### N5. Maximum entropy at fixed onset density\n\nThe orbit-Bernoulli model is the natural biased model, but is it the *only*\nextremal one?  Conjecture: among all probability distributions `P` on\n`GroupInvariantPattern G \u03b1` whose expected number of \"on\" orbits is `m \u03b8`, the\nentropy `entropyBits P` is maximized precisely by `orbitBernoulli \u03b8`, with value\n`m \u00b7 H\u2082(\u03b8)`.  *Refutation:* a group action, a `\u03b8` and a distribution with the\nsame expected onset density and strictly larger entropy.  Together with the\nproved deficit law this would make `m \u00b7 (1 - H\u2082(\u03b8))` the exact information cost\nof a stylistic onset density, rather than merely the cost of one particular\nmodel.\n",
