    "consumed_by_exp_id": "",
    "description": "# Future Directions\n\nDerived from the results proved in `Catalog/Tropical/EML/` during this cycle:\ngeneral odd/even tropical `L\u00b9` median geometry (`TropicalMedianDescent.lean`),\nperturbed and separable descent (`TropicalDescentRobustness.lean`), a kink-counting\nReLU width theory (`TropicalReluWidth.lean`), and the multi-parameter box case\n(`TropicalBoxDescent.lean`).\n\nEach conjecture below is falsifiable, and each is stated so that a Lean formalization\ncan start from the definitions already in these files (`l1Loss`, `intervalStep`,\n`projIcc`, `reluNet`, `boxLoss`).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Width equals the number of curvature sites (general PL width theorem)\n\n**Conjecture.**  Let `f : \u211d \u2192 \u211d` be continuous and piecewise linear with exactly `r`\nkinks.  Then the minimal `k` for which there exist `a b c : Fin k \u2192 \u211d` and `p q : \u211d`\nwith `reluNet a b c p q = f` is exactly `r`.\n\n*The key insight is* that `reluNet_kink_witness` already converts a nonvanishing\ndiscrete second difference into a *distinct* unit whenever the test windows are\ndisjoint, so the lower bound `r \u2264 k` needs no convexity, no differentiability, and no\nsign pattern \u2014 only separation of the kinks; the matching upper bound is the telescoping\nconstruction used in `intervalStep_eq_four_relu`.\n\n*Why now?*  This cycle proved the two smallest instances (`r = 2` for the scalar\nclipped update, `r = 4` for the interval update) with the same mechanism, and\n`descent_step_relu_width_dichotomy` shows the width is a genuine invariant of the\ntropical minimizer geometry rather than an artifact of the formula.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Tropical width spectrum of `d`-dimensional box descent\n\n**Conjecture.**  For the separable box update `boxStep lo hi \u03b7` on `d` coordinates with\n`s := #{i : lo i < hi i}` nondegenerate coordinates, the total ReLU width required to\nimplement one simultaneous step (as a map `\u211d\u1d48 \u2192 \u211d\u1d48` built from scalar units with\narbitrary affine skips) is exactly `2d + 2s`.\n\n*The key insight is* that separability makes the curvature test coordinatewise\n(`sep_minimizes_iff_coordinatewise` is the loss-side shadow of the same phenomenon), so\nthe widths add: each degenerate coordinate contributes the point-case width `2` and\neach nondegenerate coordinate the segment-case width `4`.\n\n*Why now?*  `box_minimizes_iff_mem_box` and `box_descent_reaches_minimizer` show the\n`d`-dimensional dynamics factor exactly through the `d` scalar ones, and the scalar\nwidths `2` and `4` are now theorems, so the only missing ingredient is a\n`d`-dimensional counting argument.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Perturbed descent has a sharp asymptotic radius equal to `\u03b5`\n\n**Conjecture.**  For every `0 \u2264 \u03b5 < \u03b7` and every perturbed trajectory\n(`|u\u2099\u208a\u2081 \u2212 tropicalFlow m \u03b7 u\u2099| \u2264 \u03b5`), the limit superior of `|u\u2099 \u2212 m|` is at most `\u03b5`,\nand `\u03b5` is attained: `sup over trajectories of limsup |u\u2099 \u2212 m| = \u03b5`.  Moreover the\n*loss* excess satisfies `limsup (L(u\u2099) \u2212 L(m)) = n_samples \u00b7 \u03b5` for a sample whose\nmedian has full one-sided multiplicity.\n\n*The key insight is* that the clipped update is an exact contraction to the minimizer\nin one step from distance `\u2264 \u03b7`, so the perturbation cannot accumulate: the only\nsurviving error is the last one, which is why `perturbed_distance_bound` needs `max \u03b5`\nand not `max 0`, and why `perturbed_ball_bound_sharp` saturates the bound.\n\n*Why now?*  The finite-`n` bound and its sharpness are proved; the remaining step is to\nturn them into an exact asymptotic radius and to transfer it through the proved\n`l1Loss_lipschitz` bound to the loss.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Quantile flows: the same theory for asymmetric tropical losses\n\n**Conjecture.**  Replace the tropical `L\u00b9` loss by the pinball loss\n`L\u03c4(\u03b8) = \u03a3\u1d62 \u03c1_\u03c4(\u03b8 \u2212 x\u1d62)` with `\u03c1_\u03c4(z) = max (\u03c4 z) ((\u03c4 \u2212 1) z)` for `\u03c4 \u2208 (0,1)`.  Then\nthe minimizer set is the closed interval of `\u03c4`-quantiles of the sample, and the\nassociated clipped update reaches it in `\u2308dist/\u03b7\u2309` steps, with ReLU width `2` when the\nquantile is unique and `4` when it is an interval.\n\n*The key insight is* that all proofs in this cycle used only two facts about the loss:\na *block-counting* identity (`l1Loss_growth_right/left`) and the piecewise-linear\nstructure of the update; both survive verbatim with the block sizes weighted by `\u03c4`\nand `1 \u2212 \u03c4`, which merely changes the growth slopes from `1` and `2` to `\u03c4` and\n`min \u03c4 (1\u2212\u03c4)`-type constants.\n\n*Why now?*  The counting mechanism has been isolated into two reusable lemmas that\nalready take the split index `j` as a parameter, so the quantile case is a\nre-instantiation rather than a new proof.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Non-separable tropical models: descent onto a tropical polytope\n\n**Conjecture.**  For a tropical affine model with *shared* parameters across\ncoordinates, the `L\u00b9` empirical risk is a tropical polynomial in the parameters and its\nminimizer set is a bounded tropical polytope (a finite union of alcoved polyhedra);\nclipped subgradient descent with a fixed step reaches this set in finitely many steps\nfor every positive step size, again with a projection-invariance conservation law.\n\n*The key insight is* that `projIcc`-invariance (`intervalStep_proj`) is what made\nfinite termination possible in the separable case: the projection onto the minimizer set\nis a conserved quantity of the flow, and the same conservation should hold for the\nmetric projection onto any polyhedral minimizer set of a piecewise-linear convex risk.\n\n*Why now?*  This cycle establishes the conservation law and finite termination for\npoints, segments and boxes \u2014 exactly the alcoved polytopes of dimension `0` and `1` and\ntheir products \u2014 so the general polyhedral statement is the first genuinely new case.\n\n---\n\n## Next-cycle sub-conjectures (concrete, small)\n\n1. `r`-kink lower bound for `r = 3`: the \"one-sided clipped\" update\n   `x \u21a6 min hi (max lo (x + \u03b7))` needs exactly three ReLU units.\n2. The termination time of box descent equals `max i \u2308dist_i / \u03b7\u2309` *exactly* (the\n   lower bound half is currently proved only in the odd/point case,\n   `vecStep_max_termination`).\n3. Step-size-free termination: for the *decaying* step schedule `\u03b7\u2099 = \u03b7 / (n+1)` the\n   clipped iteration diverges from finite termination (the harmonic series diverges, so\n   it still reaches the median, but only after a number of steps exponential in\n   `|x\u2080 \u2212 m| / \u03b7`); conjecturally the exact termination index is\n   `min {N : \u03a3_{n<N} \u03b7/(n+1) \u2265 |x\u2080 \u2212 m|}`, which the semigroup law\n   `tropicalFlow_trans` should reduce to a purely scalar statement.\n",
