    "description": "# Future Directions \u2014 Tropical Convexity, Helly and Optimization\n\nThis cycle proved, with zero `sorry`s:\n\n* the **tropical Cramer dependence theorem** (`trop_dependence_fin`): any `d + 1`\n  vectors of `\u211d^d` are tropically dependent, witnessed by the tropical\n  determinants of the row-deleted minors;\n* the **tropical Helly theorem with Helly number `d`** for tropical cones in\n  `\u211d^d` (`tropical_helly`, `tropical_helly_iff`) and its **sharpness**\n  (`tropical_helly_number_sharp`);\n* the **Helly number `d + 1` for tropically convex subsets of `\u211d^d`**\n  (`tropConvex_helly`) and its sharpness (`tropConvex_helly_number_sharp`),\n  which **settles the previous cycle's conjecture**: it is true for every\n  `d \u2265 1` (`tropicalHellyConjecture_holds`) with a strictly better constant than\n  the conjectured `2 * d`, and false for `d = 0`\n  (`tropicalHellyConjecture_zero`);\n* **Carath\u00e9odory number `d`** for tropical cone hulls, sharp\n  (`tropical_caratheodory_cone`, `caratheodory_cone_sharp`), and a\n  **colourful Carath\u00e9odory theorem** (`colorful_caratheodory`);\n* the optimization side: **residuation / greatest subsolution**\n  (`mulVec_le_iff_le_resid`) and the **principal-solution solvability criterion**\n  (`tropical_solvable_iff`), plus locality of tropical linear feasibility\n  (`tropical_feasibility_local`) and of difference-constraint systems\n  (`diffConstraint_feasible_iff`);\n* the **structural equivalence** `dependence_of_helly`: the Helly property, taken\n  as a hypothesis, forces tropical dependence, so the Helly theorem and the\n  Cramer dependence theorem behind it are two faces of the same statement;\n* the **boundary**: Helly fails for infinite families\n  (`tropical_helly_fails_for_infinite_families`).\n\nThe following conjectures are the concrete next steps.\n\n## Conjecture 1 (Tropical Radon number is `d + 1`)\n\n*Any `d + 1` points of `\u211d^d` can be split into two nonempty groups whose tropical\ncone hulls intersect.*\n\n**The key insight is** that a Radon partition is exactly a proper 2-colouring of\nthe *argmax hypergraph* `{M_i}` of a dependence witness `lam` (edge `M_i` = set\nof rows attaining the maximum in coordinate `i`): the partition works iff every\n`M_i` is bichromatic.  The Cramer witness of this cycle already forces\n`|M_i| \u2265 2`, but a hypergraph with `d` edges of size `\u2265 2` on `d + 1` vertices\ncan fail property B (a triangle plus isolated vertices), so the conjecture needs\nan *optimisation over the whole dependence polytope*\n`\u039b = {lam : every column maximum attained twice}` rather than one point of it.\n**Why now?** `\u039b` is a nonempty polyhedral complex by this cycle's theorem, so the\nquestion is now a concrete finite optimisation over an explicitly constructed\nobject, and Levi's inequality (`Helly \u2264 Radon \u2212 1`) is already tight at `d` on\nour extremal family, which is exactly what a Radon number `d + 1` predicts.\n\n## Conjecture 2 (Colourful tropical Helly)\n\n*Let `F_1, \u2026, F_d` be finite families (\"colours\") of tropical cones in `\u211d^d`.  If\nevery rainbow selection `C_1 \u2208 F_1, \u2026, C_d \u2208 F_d` has a common point, then some\nsingle colour `F_c` has a common point.*\n\n**The key insight is** that the colourful Carath\u00e9odory theorem proved here has an\nexceptionally simple tropical proof \u2014 coordinate `c` is served by colour `c` \u2014\nwhich suggests a matching \"one coordinate per colour\" argument on the Helly side,\nwith the argmax coordinate playing the role of B\u00e1r\u00e1ny's rotation argument.\n**Why now?** The uncoloured case is settled with the optimal constant `d`, and\nthe colourful Carath\u00e9odory statement it needs as input is now a theorem, so the\nonly missing ingredient is the colourful analogue of the dependence witness.\n\n## Conjecture 3 (Helly over the full max-plus semiring `\u211d_max`)\n\n*The Helly number of tropically convex subsets of `(\u211d \u222a {\u2212\u221e})^d` is still `d`.*\n\n**The key insight is** that the whole Cramer argument is semiring-theoretic: the\ntropical determinant, the Laplace expansion and the two-equal-columns swap all\nmake sense in `\u211d_max`, provided the degenerate case \"all permutation weights are\n`\u2212\u221e`\" is handled by a support/matching argument (Hall's theorem on the bipartite\nsupport graph).  **Why now?** The `\u211d`-valued proof is complete and modular: only\n`sum_augCol`, `weight_le_cramerWeight` and the swap lemma touch arithmetic, so\nthe extension is a controlled re-run in `WithBot \u211d` plus one Hall-type lemma.\n\n## Conjecture 4 (Certificate complexity of tropical infeasibility is exactly `d`)\n\n*For every `n > d` there is a system of `n` tropical halfspaces in `d` variables\nthat is infeasible, every `d \u2212 1` of whose members are feasible, and for which no\ninfeasibility certificate of size `< d` exists; moreover deciding feasibility of\n`n` halfspaces is polynomially equivalent to a mean-payoff game.*\n\n**The key insight is** that our extremal family `{x : \u2203 j \u2260 k, x_k + 1 \u2264 x_j}`\nconsists of tropical halfspaces with *finite* coefficients, so the Helly bound\n`d` is attained inside the halfspace class itself; the game-theoretic half of the\nstatement should follow from the residuation Galois connection proved here, whose\nfixed points are exactly the optimal strategies.  **Why now?** Both ingredients \u2014\nsharp Helly and the principal-solution criterion \u2014 are now formalised, so the\nstatement reduces to a formalised reduction rather than new geometry.\n\n## Conjecture 5 (Fractional / `(p, q)` tropical Helly)\n\n*If among `n` tropical cones in `\u211d^d` a fraction `\u03b1` of the `d`-tuples intersect,\nthen some `f(\u03b1, d) \u00b7 n` of them have a common point.*\n\n**The key insight is** that the tropical Helly proof is *constructive and local*:\nthe common point of a `d`-tuple is an explicit max-plus combination of the\nwitnesses, so a counting argument over argmax patterns (there are at most\n`(d+1)^d` of them) should convert local intersection density into a large\nintersecting subfamily without any topological input.  **Why now?** The classical\nfractional Helly theorem needs the topology of `\u211d^d`; the tropical proof here is\npurely combinatorial, which is precisely the regime where a fractional version\nshould be provable by pigeonhole on the finitely many argmax patterns.\n",
