    "description": "# FUTURE DIRECTIONS \u2014 Algorithmic Immune Systems\n\nDerived from the verified results in `Catalog/Shared/Immune*.lean` (Parts I\u2013IX:\nparasite calculus and attestation, semantics, the diagonal parasite, quarantine\nand the conservation law, the reflexive oracle barrier, the algebra of mutations\nand the immune uncertainty principle, ensembles and the arms race, bounded\nuniverses, monitoring frequency).\n\nEach conjecture below is stated so that it can be *falsified* by a single Lean\ncounterexample.\n\n---\n\n## Conjecture 1 (Immune capacity law: rigidity \u00d7 memory is exactly exponential)\n\nFor every monitor `S \u2286 PAst` and every size bound `N`, let `mem(S) = |S|` and let\n`rig(S, N)` be the number of behaviourally trivial programs of size `\u2264 N` that\n`S` rejects.  Then there are absolute constants `c\u2081, c\u2082 > 0` with\n\n`c\u2081 \u00b7 2^{N/3} \u2264 mem(S) + rig(S, N) \u2264 c\u2082 \u00b7 2^{N/3} \u00b7 poly(N)` for every *optimal*\nmonitor, and the lower bound is attained only by the bounded whitelist of\nPart VIII.\n\n*Status.* The lower bound `2^n \u2264 |S| + |padFamily n \\ S|` is **proved**\n(`immune_uncertainty`); the matching upper bound and the uniqueness of the\noptimum are open.\n\n**The key insight is** that `pad` realises an *injective encoding of bit strings\ninto a single semantic equivalence class*, so the immune system is forced to pay\none bit of memory per bit of dead code it wishes to tolerate \u2014 attestation is a\nlossless code for a class on which behaviour is constant.\n\n**Why now?** Both sides are finitary and decidable for fixed `N`: the upper bound\nis a counting argument over `astUniverse N L`, which is already constructed and\nproved to contain the bounded universe (`mem_astUniverse`).\n\n---\n\n## Conjecture 2 (Reflexive oracle hierarchy)\n\nStratify programs by *reflexion depth*: `ask`-free programs have depth `0`, and a\nprogram has depth `\u2264 d+1` if every oracle query it makes is answered by an oracle\nthat is correct on all programs of depth `\u2264 d`.  Then for every `d` there is an\noracle `O_d` correct on all programs of depth `\u2264 d`, no oracle is correct at\ndepth `d+1` for all `d` simultaneously, and the hierarchy is strict.\n\n*Status.* Depth `0` is **proved** (`oracle_correct_on_askFree`), and the global\nimpossibility is **proved** (`no_correct_reflexive_oracle`).  The strictness of\nthe intermediate levels is open.\n\n**The key insight is** that oracle-independence of `ask`-free behaviour\n(`askFree_effect_oracle_indep`) is the base case of an induction on reflexion\ndepth: each level fixes the semantics of the level below, exactly as a Tarskian\ntruth hierarchy escapes the liar by stratification.\n\n**Why now?** The oracle-parameterised semantics `evalO`/`effectO` is already in\nplace, so a depth predicate is a routine inductive definition on `OAst`, and the\nlevel-`d` oracle can be defined by the same classical comprehension used for\n`canonicalOracle`.\n\n---\n\n## Conjecture 3 (No probabilistic escape from the diagonal)\n\nLet `\u03bc` be any finitely supported probability distribution over harmless\ndetectors, and let `err(\u03bc) = inf_p Pr_{d ~ \u03bc}[d classifies p correctly]`.  Then\n`err(\u03bc) = 0`: there is a single program on which *every* detector in the support\nerrs, so randomisation does not buy even an `\u03b5` advantage.\n\n*Status.* The support-wise version is **proved** for sound detectors\n(`ensemble_common_escape`, `ensemble_vote_zero`: the vote count for the escaping\nparasite is exactly `0`).  The general case, where members may be unsound, is\nopen and is the interesting one.\n\n**The key insight is** that the disjunctive ensemble `ensembleOr` is itself a\nprogram of the calculus, so the diagonal construction applies to the *ensemble*,\nnot to its members; randomisation over a finite support is subsumed by a single\ndeterministic program.\n\n**Why now?** `ensembleOr` with `flags_ensembleOr_iff` already reduces any monotone\ncombination rule to a single detector; the remaining work is to handle non-monotone\nrules (majority with unsound members) by a counting argument over the support.\n\n---\n\n## Conjecture 4 (Latency\u2013damage law for sampled monitoring)\n\nFor monitoring period `k` and any horizon `T`, the maximal number of compromised\nsteps that an adversary can force is exactly `T - \u230aT/k\u230b`, and this is attained by\nthe constant `attack` adversary; moreover no rollback policy weaker than\nper-step verification changes this count.\n\n*Status.* Both extremes are **proved**: `periodic_healing` (clean at every\ncheckpoint) and `attack_window` (compromised at every non-checkpoint), which\nalready pin the count for the constant adversary.  The optimality over *all*\npolicies is open.\n\n**The key insight is** that quarantine is an idempotent retraction\n(`quarantine_idem`), so the guarded dynamics is completely determined by the\ncheckpoint pattern; the damage count is therefore a purely combinatorial function\nof the sampling set, independent of the adversary's cleverness.\n\n**Why now?** `traceK` generalises verbatim to an arbitrary checkpoint set\n`C \u2286 \u2115`, turning the conjecture into a statement about `|[0,T] \\ C|` that should\nfollow from the same case analysis used in `attack_window`.\n\n---\n\n## Conjecture 5 (Semantic quotient collapse)\n\nLet `PAst/\u2248` be the quotient by semantic equivalence (`semSetoid`).  Then no\nfinite monitor on the quotient can exist at all: every `\u2248`-class that contains a\nmalicious program contains programs of unbounded size, and any monitor that is\n`\u2248`-invariant, sound and computable must accuse either nothing or everything \u2014\nthe categorical shadow of `no_perfect_detector`.\n\n*Status.* Open.  The ingredients are proved: classes are exponentially large\n(`semClass_card_exp`), finite whitelists are never `\u2248`-closed\n(`finite_whitelist_not_semantically_closed`), and the internal/external gap is\nisolated (`internal_external_gap`).\n\n**The key insight is** that `\u2248`-invariance is precisely the hypothesis Rice's\ntheorem needs, while attestation deliberately violates it; the immune system's\npower comes entirely from *not* being a semantic invariant.\n\n**Why now?** `semSetoid` is already available as a `Setoid`, so the quotient type\nand the induced monitor are one definition away, and the two horns of the\ndichotomy can be assembled from `sound_detector_misses` and\n`complete_detector_false_alarms`.\n\n---\n\n## Three concrete next-cycle sub-conjectures\n\n1. **(C1a)** `|astUniverse N L| \u2264 (L + 2)^{2^{O(N)}}` is far too weak; the true\n   count of programs of size `\u2264 N` with literals `< L` satisfies a Catalan-type\n   recurrence.  Formalise the recurrence and derive a *matching* upper bound for\n   Conjecture 1.\n2. **(C2a)** Define reflexion depth on `OAst` and prove level `1`: there is an\n   oracle correct on all programs whose `ask` arguments are themselves\n   `ask`-free.\n3. **(C4a)** Replace `traceK` by checkpoints indexed by an arbitrary set `C` and\n   prove `damage(C, T) = |[1,T] \\ C|` for the constant `attack` adversary.\n",
