    "description": "# Future Directions\n\nConjectures distilled from the formalization of *Various Bialgebras of\nRepresentative Functions on Free Monoids* carried out in `Catalog/Novelty/`\n(`FreeMonoidShuffle`, `FreeMonoidUnshuffle`, `FreeMonoidCharacters`,\n`RepresentativeFunctions`, `DeconcatenationShuffle`,\n`ShuffleCharacterNotRational`, `ShuffleOfSeries`).\n\nEach conjecture below is stated so that it can be turned directly into a Lean\nstatement over the existing definitions, and each is falsifiable by an explicit\nfinite computation or by exhibiting a single counterexample.\n\n---\n\n## C1. The antipode of the shuffle Hopf algebra is the signed reversal\n\n**Statement.** Over the definitions `shuf` (shuffle) and `deconc`\n(deconcatenation coproduct) of `Catalog/Novelty/`, for every nonempty word `w`\nand every field `K \u2287 \u211a`,\n`\u03a3_{(u,v) \u2208 deconc w} (-1)^{|u|} \u00b7 (count z (shuf (reverse u) v)) = 0` for all\n`z`, i.e. `S(w) = (-1)^{|w|} \u00b7 reverse w` is the antipode of the graded Hopf\nalgebra `(K\u27e8X\u27e9, \u29e2, \u0394_deconc)`.\n\n*The key insight is* that the already-proved bialgebra axiom\n`deconc_bind_shuf` upgrades to a Hopf structure precisely because the\ndeconcatenation coproduct is connected and graded, so the antipode is forced by\nTakeuchi's recursion \u2014 and the closed form must then be a *signed multiset\nidentity between shuffles of reversals*, which is a purely combinatorial claim\namenable to the counting machinery (`count_shuf_eq_count_unsh`,\n`count_deconc`) already developed here.\n\n*Why now?* All of the counting infrastructure for `shuf`, `unsh` and `deconc`\nnow exists and is verified; the antipode is the last missing structure map, and\nit is exactly the input needed to state Sweedler duality intrinsically.\n\n---\n\n## C2. Rational series form a shuffle-subalgebra that is *not* closed under\nthe antipode-twisted inverse\n\n**Statement.** `isRepresentative_shuffleSeries` shows rationality is preserved by\n`\u29e2`. Conjecture: the shuffle-invertible rational series (those `f` with\n`f [] \u2260 0`) do **not** form a group inside the rational series: there is a\nrational `f` with `f [] = 1` whose shuffle inverse `g` (which exists uniquely as\na series) has infinite Hankel rank.\n\n*The key insight is* that the separation already proved in\n`ShuffleCharacterNotRational` \u2014 `expPlane` is a shuffle character but has\ninfinite Hankel rank because `det[1/(i+j)!] \u2260 0` \u2014 should be reachable from a\n*rational* input by shuffle inversion, since the shuffle inverse of `1 - x` type\nseries is an exponential-like series with factorial denominators.\n\n*Why now?* `factorial_relation_vanishes` gives a working, Archimedean method for\nproving infinite Hankel rank; the same method should apply verbatim to the\ncoefficients of a shuffle inverse.\n\n---\n\n## C3. \u03c6-deformations interpolate between concatenation and shuffle without\nchanging the rational locus\n\n**Statement.** For a parameter `q : K`, define the `q`-shuffle on words by the\nrecursion `au \u29e2_q bv = a(u \u29e2_q bv) + b(au \u29e2_q v) + q \u00b7 [a=b] \u00b7 \u27e8ab\u27e9(u \u29e2_q v)`.\nConjecture: for every `q`, `(K\u27e8X\u27e9, \u29e2_q)` is associative and commutative, and\nthe set of representative functions is closed under `\u29e2_q` for every `q`, i.e.\nthe rational locus is a *deformation invariant*.\n\n*The key insight is* that the proof of `isRepresentative_shuffleSeries` uses\nonly the bialgebra axiom `unsh_append` for the dual coproduct, never the precise\ncombinatorics of the shuffle; so any deformation whose dual coproduct is still\nmultiplicative for concatenation must preserve rationality.\n\n*Why now?* The proof in `ShuffleOfSeries.lean` is already written in exactly this\n\"axiom-only\" style, so the deformed case should require only a new\n`unsh_q_append` lemma and nothing else.\n\n---\n\n## C4. A Ree-type criterion: rational shuffle characters are exactly the\nexponentials of rational planes \u2014 and there are none but the counit\n\n**Statement.** If `f` is a shuffle character (`f(u)f(v) = \u03a3_{w \u2208 u \u29e2 v} f(w)`)\nand `f` is representative, then `f = counit` whenever the alphabet is nonempty\nand `K` has characteristic 0.\n\n*The key insight is* that `isConcatCharacter_iff_planeStar` and\n`isConcatInfChar_iff_isPlane` say a character is determined by a single plane,\nand the plane's exponential has factorial coefficients \u2014 the very coefficients\nproved non-rational in `ShuffleCharacterNotRational`. The partial results\n`planeStar_isShuffleCharacter_imp_zero` and `not_isRepresentative_expPlane`\nalready close the two extreme cases.\n\n*Why now?* Only the \"every shuffle character is the exponential of its\ninfinitesimal part\" step (a Ree-type theorem over \u211a) is missing; the rest is\nverified.\n\n---\n\n## C5. Sweedler duality is an isomorphism onto the representative functions\n\n**Statement.** The map sending a linear representation `(\u03bb, \u03bc, \u03b3)` to the series\n`w \u21a6 \u03bb \u03bc(w) \u03b3` induces a bijection between the finite-dimensional comodule\nstructures on `K\u27e8X\u27e9` (for `\u0394_conc`) and the space of representative functions,\nand it is an algebra isomorphism for both the Hadamard and the shuffle products.\n\n*The key insight is* that `representative_tfae` already identifies \"finite\ndimensional space of left translates\" with \"has a linear representation\"; adding\nthe shuffle multiplicativity `isRepresentative_shuffleSeries` upgrades this\nbijection from a linear isomorphism to a bialgebra isomorphism \u2014 the Sweedler\ndual statement of the paper.\n\n*Why now?* Both halves (Kleene\u2013Sch\u00fctzenberger and shuffle closure) are now\nformalized and sorry-free; only the naturality of the correspondence remains.\n",
