    "description": "# Future directions \u2014 bold, testable conjectures from the A\u2084 fork-pinning cycle\n\nThe formal cycle established: (i) the pinned/flat/leaking **trichotomy** for an\narbitrary finite dial (`info_trichotomy`), (ii) the **exact leakage law**\n`I = H(pq) \u2212 p\u00b7H(q)` and its `k`-factor version, (iii) the group side\n`V\u2084 = [A\u2084,A\u2084]`, `|A\u2084^ab| = 3`, within-`V\u2084` flatness, (iv) the arithmetic side\n(Klein resolvent `y\u00b3\u221248y\u221264 = 64((y/4)\u00b3\u22123(y/4)\u22121)`, conductor `9`, cubes mod 9),\n(v) the abelianisation criterion `FactorsThroughAb \u2194 commutator-invariance`, with\n`A\u2085` absolutely unpinnable.  The following are the next falsifiable steps.\n\n## C1. The conductor\u2013order dictionary: `I = H(1/m)` iff the fork is a fibre of an order-`m` quotient\n\n**Conjecture.** Let `L/\u211a` be Galois with group `G`, let `N \u22b4 G` with `G/N` cyclic\nof order `m`, and let `F = [Frob \u2208 N]`.  Then `F` is pinned by the character of\nconductor `f(G/N)` and `I(p mod f ; F) = H(1/m)` exactly; conversely, if a fork\nof rate `1/m` attains `I = H(1/m)` for some modulus, its defining set is a union\nof fibres of a cyclic quotient of order `m`.\n\n*The key insight is* that the entropy value `H(1/m)` is not a coincidence of the\ncubic case: it is the entropy of the uniform distribution on the fibres of\n`G \u21a0 G^ab \u21a0 C_m`, and the trichotomy theorem already forces saturation to be\nequivalent to determinism, so only the *rate* survives as an invariant.\n*Why now?* Both halves are now formal objects: `info_eq_top_iff` supplies the\nconverse direction abstractly, and `factorsThroughAb_iff` supplies the group\nside; only the Artin/Chebotarev bridge remains to be axiomatised or imported.\n\n## C2. Universal leakage spectrum of a Galois group\n\n**Conjecture.** For a fixed `G`, the set of achievable pairs\n`(rate, information)` over *all* conjugation-stable forks and *all* moduli is the\nfinite set `{(|S|/|G|, H(pq) \u2212 p\u00b7H(q)) : S a union of G^ab-fibres thinned by a\nG-orbit}` \u2014 in particular it is contained in the curve family\n`I = H(pq) \u2212 p\u00b7H(q)` with `p \u2208 (1/[G:G'])\u00b7\u2124` and `q \u2208 (1/|G'|)\u00b7\u2124`.\n\n*The key insight is* that every fork factors as (pinned part) \u2218 (flat thinning),\nbecause the commutator subgroup acts transitively on the ambiguity: the leakage\nlaw is not one example but a normal form.\n*Why now?* `info_leak`, `info_leak_strict` and `abelian_hom_eq_one_on_V4` give\nthe two extremes; the missing step is a decomposition lemma \"every fork is a\n`q`-thinning of its `G^ab`-saturation\", which is a finite-group statement.\n\n## C3. `A\u2085` gives an unconditional information wall\n\n**Conjecture.** For the splitting field of a quintic with `Gal = A\u2085` and *any*\nmodulus `m`, *every* splitting fork satisfies `I(p mod m ; F) = 0`, i.e. the\nfactorisation type of `p` is statistically independent of every congruence class.\n\n*The key insight is* that `A\u2085` is perfect, so the only abelian data attached to\n`Frob` is trivial \u2014 already proved here as `A5_absolutely_unpinnable`; what\nremains is to convert \"no abelian character sees it\" into \"zero mutual\ninformation\", i.e. equidistribution of Frobenius within each ray class.\n*Why now?* `A5_fork_factors_iff_constant` shows the group side is closed; the\nanalytic side is exactly Chebotarev for the compositum with `\u211a(\u03b6_m)`.\n\n## C4. Collapse rate of the multiplicative channel\n\n**Conjecture.** For `N` a product of `k` unramified primes of the `A\u2084`-field,\nthe mutual information between `N mod 9` and the full split-vector satisfies\n`I_k = \u0398(k\u00b73^{-k})` for the \"all split\" fork and `I_k \u2192 H(Bin-class)` for the\ncount fork; in particular the *per-factor* information tends to `0`\ngeometrically, quantifying \"factor-useless\".\n\n*The key insight is* that thinning by `3^{-(k-1)}` sends the leakage law into the\nregime `H(pq) \u2212 pH(q) \u2248 pq\u00b7log\u2082(1/p)`, which is linear in `q`; the proved limit\n`info_all_split_tendsto_zero` is the qualitative shadow of that asymptotic.\n*Why now?* The exact `k`-dependent closed form `H(3^{-(k+1)}) \u2212 (1/3)H(3^{-k})`\nis already formal, so the conjecture is now a pure asymptotic analysis exercise\nabout `H` near `0`.\n\n## C5. Minimal conductor is detected by information alone\n\n**Conjecture.** For a pinned fork with cyclic quotient of order `m` and conductor\n`f`, the function `m' \u21a6 I(p mod m' ; F)` is `0` for every `m'` with `f \u2224 m'`, and\nequals `H(1/m)` for every multiple of `f`: the information profile is a\n*characteristic function of the divisibility relation*, so the conductor is\nrecoverable from entropy measurements without any algebraic input.\n\n*The key insight is* that a non-multiple of the conductor intersects every fibre\nof the ray-class group in equal proportion, which is exactly the \"flat\" branch of\nthe trichotomy \u2014 the mod-3 blindness proved in `mod_three_flat` is the smallest\ninstance.\n*Why now?* `info_of_flat` and `info_of_pinned` are proved, and `mod_three_flat`\nshows the CRT mechanism at the conductor's own prime; the general statement is a\nfinite computation in `(\u2124/lcm)\u02e3`.\n",
